   $q$Read the words: "Because the river had risen after three days of rain." Which revision turns this fragment into a complete sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Because the river had risen, after three days of rain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-comma-only"},{"text":"Because the river had risen after three days of rain and the bridge.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-words-not-clause"},{"text":"Because the river had risen after three days of rain, the ranger closed the bridge.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Because the river, which had risen after three days of rain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-another-dependent-part"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because the river had risen after three days of rain, the ranger closed the bridge.$q$, $q$A clause that starts with "because" needs a main clause to finish the thought, and "the ranger closed the bridge" provides one. Adding a comma alone does not help, because the words still do not express a complete thought.$q$, 'draft', null)
